From: DE25-Nano Port <de25-nano@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Disable unavailable DE25 DDR save states

MiSTer cores advertise save-state storage in the upper half of the DE10-Nano's
1 GiB DDR window. The current DE25 platform has 512 MiB of LPDDR and no remapped
core-DDR aperture. Mapping a typical core's logical 0x3E000000 save-state area
therefore reaches unpopulated physical memory and raises SIGBUS.

Disable the optional HPS-managed save-state buffer on DE25 until the common
shell implements a bounded DDR aperture. Core ROM transfer and gameplay use
the separate SPI path and remain available.

diff --git a/user_io.cpp b/user_io.cpp
--- a/user_io.cpp
+++ b/user_io.cpp
@@ -1077,6 +1077,19 @@ static void parse_config()
 		ss_base = 0x3E000000;
 		ss_size = 0x100000;
 	}
+
+#ifdef MISTER_DE25
+	// DE10 cores place save states in the upper half of a 1 GiB DDR window.
+	// DE25 currently exposes 512 MiB of LPDDR and has no remapped core-DDR
+	// aperture, so HPS access to that advertised address would raise SIGBUS.
+	if (ss_base)
+	{
+		printf("DE25: disabling unsupported DDR save-state buffer at 0x%X.\n",
+			ss_base);
+		ss_base = 0;
+		ss_size = 0;
+	}
+#endif
 }
 
 //MSM6242B layout
